Greedily change the right character of each conflicting pair, then skip it so the edit cannot create another conflict with the next character.
```python
class Solution:
    def remove almostEqualCharacters(self, word: str) -> int:
        count = i = 0
        while i + 1 < len(word):
            if abs(ord(word[i]) - ord(word[i + 1])) <= 1:
                count += 1
                i += 2
            else:
                i += 1
        return count
```
